# Polymorphic prelude functions work correctly with typed arguments.
# Exercises map, filter, and fold (higher-order prelude functions) end-to-end,
# verifying that the %rust pseudo-module registration fix enables correct
# prelude typechecking so polymorphic functions retain their types.
# No === warn section: clean code must produce zero type warnings.
[add-one:  [fn [let x@Int] [+ x 1]]
 mapped:   [map add-one [1 2 3]]
 filtered: [filter [fn [let x] [< x 3]] [1 2 3 4 5]]
 sum:      [fold [fn [let acc x] [+ acc x]] 0 [1 2 3 4 5]]]
=== out
Dict({"add-one": Function(x), "mapped": Dict({0: Int(2), 1: Int(3), 2: Int(4)}), "filtered": Seq(Int(1), ...), "sum": Int(15)})
